    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 7 USER]\ne060\tMy provisional plan is to offer Northline three focused sessions over the next two weeks, document the workflow, and explicitly make no build commitment.\ne061\tLina can lead the sessions but not start production code.\ne062\tIn the same period we will define the reliability work and the core-workflow release we are actually willing to promise.\ne063\tThen we decide with all three pieces visible.\ne064\tI still worry that “no production code” wastes Lina's best way of learning and that Northline will hear a polite no.\ne065\tBut starting the build now feels less defensible than it did.\n[Turn 7 ASSISTANT]\ne066\tThat plan protects the learning opportunity without pretending the underlying tradeoff is resolved.\ne067\tThe two risks you named remain real: restricting prototypes may make discovery artificial, while careful language may still feel like distance to Northline.\ne068\tYou can decide in advance what kind of disposable prototype is allowed and ask Northline to reflect back what they believe the sessions mean.\ne069\tNeither step guarantees trust or a good product decision, but both make misunderstanding easier to notice before momentum chooses for you.",
